{
"opening": "This release introduces several new functions and improves existing ones to enhance the library's utility for functional programming tasks. It also updates compatibility and performance characteristics across key modules.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m02",
"text": "The public API must expose a function named compose_left that accepts an iterable of functions and returns a new function representing their left-to-right composition."
},
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The public API must expose a function named peekn that takes an integer n and an iterable, yielding the first n items while consuming them from the input iterator."
},
{
"id": "m04",
"text": "The dissoc function must perform dictionary deletion operations with optimized performance compared to previous versions, maintaining its standard signature and return value."
},
{
"id": "m05",
"text": "The public API must expose a class or callable named Compose that supports function composition, ensuring it behaves consistently with the existing compose function but potentially offering enhanced features or interface."
},
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "The fold function must support parallel execution capabilities, allowing it to process iterables using multiple workers while maintaining deterministic results based on the associative operator provided."
},
{
"id": "m14",
"text": "The merge and merge_with functions must accept any Mapping type as input, not just dict instances, and return a merged mapping of the same type as the first argument."
},
{
"id": "m18",
"text": "All listed functions must operate exclusively in Python 3 environments, removing any legacy Python 2 specific code paths or syntax, and raising appropriate errors if invoked in incompatible contexts."
},
{
"id": "m28",
"text": "The library must provide correct type signatures and runtime behavior for Python 3.10, specifically supporting the anext built-in function where applicable in relevant toolz wrappers."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all changes are reflected in the public namespace and documentation accordingly."
}
